10/26/96  Added global variable for HermSetup and removed the variable from where its           passed to most of the routines.10/28/96  Turned on all error checking for pascal compiler.  Removed all unused variables           from function/procedures and parameters.  Also found a bad FOR loop at bottom           of the procedure EncodeString.  For loop index is being modified inside for           loop.  Need to use debugger to see whats really happening in this loop.  Could          be delicate to change since this is used to check the registration string.            Should maybe change this to a while loop to protect against compiler           optimization.10/30/96  Added UFailure unit and did some simple testing to see if it worked properly.  This          unit provides a mechanism for error handling which is similair to using a           try/catch block in C++.  See UFailure.p for a more complete description.10/31/96  Added FailNIL call at each memory allocation with NewHandle or NewPointer.            Added FailOSErr call to each system call.  Could possibly add some           preflighting to catch potential errors while resource is loading.  This           required some additional units and also required some changes to the privates           handle.  The handle was separated into two parts.  The first part saves flow           control info, and the second part saves external data.  The second part is           contained in the first part as a handle.  Separation of these parts will allow           the UFailure unit to easily be transferred and used in any other external           (such as SlySysop).  Added global variables for each type of privates.  The           globals are setup for each time the external is called.11/1/96   Moved case for each stage into its own procedure.  This allowed a single case           statement to be used for all stages instead of keeping the setup that was           necessary when compiling multiple resources to get around the 32 K barrior.            Also added a constant for each stage to make the code more readable.  During           the process, many of the Hermes callbacks were changed to use the gHermSetup           global variable.  Also added some functions to simpify accessing hermes data           structures.  These routines were placed in the ExternalUtils file.  Changed           the segmentation so those procedures handling states were in one segment, and           their utility helpers were in another. Other small fixups are too numerous to           remember.11/15/96  After working on the monster names, it appears it may be easiest to add another          option for each monster -- an action string.  This would make it so Elementals          wouldn't have to "wave" things at you.  Instead they could "send" things at          you.  Others could "point" things at you.  Since were going to have to change           the data format for monsters, this appears to be a good time to change to C++.          This is where the work is headed now.  Also began working on building an object          oriented framework for externals.  For now, there are only two objects:           TExternals, and TPrivates.  As it stands, this makes it easier to begin writing          a new external.  There are only a few routines to override to make your Prefs           and Privates.  This makes it so you can dig right into making all those stage           additions.  Also changed the SlySysOp external so it uses the framework.11/22/96  External has been changed to C++.  This definately added several bugs, but it          appears most have been fixed now.  It is now much better to add the proper type          of error handling using C++ try/catch blocks.  Upon fixing bugs, it was           difficult to follow the file handling routines.  In particular, the routines           for a PlayerList and CharacterRec (CharRec).  An object (TFile) was added to           handle basic file handling, and a template (TItemFile<ItemType>) was added to           allow higher level routines for reading and writing to files.  This will           hopefully allow for file versions to be easily added to the data files.  One           potential problem area that still remains is that a single file could be           required to be open twice at once by both Slycrel and SlySysop.  Need to find           a way to comunicate between externals or handle files independently of both           externals.  Changed algorithm for firing arrow. It was changed because the           external was mysteriously writing junk after firing a certain number of times.          The real reason was because a const StringPtr was being modified in TextOut.          Need to be careful where const StringPtrs are passed.  Need to go through           routines to see where constants are being passed and change parameters to           const parameters.  Did this, but not sure I got 'em all.          11/26/96  Added beginning menu selection to edit character information.  Used code for          creating a character.  Added monster new monster names in text file format.            Binary monster files are created from the text files.  Added all missing menus.          Included were [C]haracter info at start menu.  Not sure how well changing your          name will be handled.  [J]ail, [S]mith's Blacksmith, [@]Tower of Wisdom,           [L]isten to rumors, [T]alk to inkeep, [L]ook around, and [V]iew something.            All additions just included text messages and modification of weapons or           character attributes.  Also added were the combat menus [S]pecial, [U]se Item,           [E]xamine.  These just used text messages as well.         12/2/96   Finally bit the bullet and combined PlayerList and individual CharacterRec           files to a single file.  This makes the file handling code easier to follow.            Also cleaned up the code for displaying high scores so it always displays           properly.  Not sure exactly how much these changes will slow down the code           when searching for a CharacterRec, but since this only happens at the           beginning of the game it should be no major problem.  Also, the search was           previously done anyway, now we just read in a few more bytes while doing it.            Game now appears to be quite stable.                    Fixed nagging bug in terrain editor.  When first character in row was nothing,          remaining characters would be off by one position.  Also added a menu at           startup and when [R]etrieving a file to select the files from.  Also added the           filename to the editing display.  Added a "dirty" private variable which is           set to true when terrain is changed in any way.  Use this variable to ask if           file to be saved when quiting or retrieving another file.  Terrain editor was           changed to C some time ago.          12/3/96   Fixed monster/user strings in STR# resources so they are complete and print           during text combat.  Made final non-debugging copies of each external and did           simple tests to make sure no new bugs crept in.  Began preparing documentation           to ship new version.  This will be 2.51!